      "content": "Your overwhelming self-criticism is a dangerous symptom of trauma, not an accurate reflection of your soul, and imagining your absence would not truly balance the world because genuine connection requires the messy, broken humans like you who show up anyway. Sometimes the harshest judgment you ever voice is not from others, but from the very pain that left you feeling numb in the hallway, and learning to trust that feeling again is the only path to healing. If the idea of staying \"balanced\" feels impossible, please reach out to a crisis line where someone can sit with you in the silence until you feel strong enough to be human again.",
